From ccb545d8930d04e28e1b1b569e0bd1c77494d03e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:53:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 023/100] data: play property keyframe animations the way
 Wallpaper Engine does

A property's `animation` (`{"c0": [keys], ..., "options": {...},
"relative": ...}` next to its `value`) was never read, so every animated
fade, move, spin and effect constant stood still at its value. They now
play, as decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485 (parser 0x1401d1740, curves
0x1401d4dd0, options 0x1401d5790/0x1401d4d00, wraploop 0x1401d5990, curve
bake 0x1401d5c50, clock 0x1401d6a00, sampler in 0x1401a19e0):

- Curves c0..c3, one per component, in order (a missing one ends the
  list; a component without a curve keeps its value). A key is
  {frame, value, back, front, step}; a handle is an object, enabled
  unless `"enabled": false` (a disabled one is (0, 0)); keys whose frame
  doesn't move forward are dropped.
- Between keys A and B: a cubic bezier through (0, A.value),
  (A.front.x / 2, A.value + A.front.y), (1 + B.back.x / 2,
  B.value + B.back.y), (1, B.value) over the normalised segment, x solved
  by up to 24 Newton steps inside a bisection bracket (tolerance
  max(0.01 / segment frames, FLT_EPSILON)). All four handle numbers zero,
  or both control points on the line, is linear. A `step` B holds A's
  value; before the first key and after the last, the end values hold.
- Evaluated at whole frames and blended linearly between frame n and
  n + 1 by the time left over.
- `options`: fps > 0 and length > 0 (frames) or there's no animation;
  mode `loop` (default), `mirror` (ping-pong), `single` (plays once,
  holds); `startpaused` never advances (nothing can play() it yet:
  SceneScript's getAnimation is not there); `wraploop` drops keys past
  `length` and puts a key at `length` that copies the first one (value,
  step, its front handle mirrored as the back handle).
- `relative`: c0..c2 are offsets added to the value when the value is an
  "x y z" string (WE adds nothing to a numeric value).

Values parsed with an animation while a scene is parsed are listed on the
Scene (an AnimationCollector), with the value's alive flag; every frame,
before the script tick (so a script's update(value) gets the animated
value), CScene advances each by the frame's dt of the host clock and
writes it (UpdateSource::Animation). Object values (alpha, origin,
angles, scale, colour) and effect constants are covered alike.

Not done: `timeofday` mode, `options.parent`/`children` shared
timelines (each property runs its own, from the same start, so they stay
in step until a script controls one), `random`, animation events and the
SceneScript animation API (getAnimation, play/stop/pause, setFrame).

Origin: ours
Why: keyframe animations were ignored in lp-player: animated fades, moves, rotations and effect values static in 26 of the owner's scenes (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B2: G01, G02)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8YtBieDNWXo3bvfKaP
